Appendix M — Immediate Scientific Object

The first thing to compute:

\inf_{P \in \mathcal{M}_A} I_P(T; X_i \mid X_S) \quad \text{and} \quad \sup_{P \in \mathcal{M}_A} I_P(T; X_i \mid X_S)

on the binary toy (T, X_1, X_2) \in \{0,1\}^3, under the corrected specification ladder A_0 \subset A_1 \subset A_2 \subset A_3 \subset A_4 \subset A_5, with A_4 including a reliability constraint coupling T to X_i.

The question:

\boxed{\text{Is there a rung } A_k \text{ at which } \Delta_i^-(S;A_k) > 0 \text{ and } \widetilde W_i(S;A_k) < \tau?}

If yes, the framework has a non-vacuous robust-information core, and the next step is the minimal experiment of Appendix H.

If no, the framework must be redesigned before any empirical claim.

The ladder is the gate. Face the death test first. 🌹

