13. The Delta- = 0 Pathology

```
  CASE 1: attributionally fragile  ( d- = 0 )
  ---------------------------------------------
      P0 in M :  I_{P0}(T ; Y | X)  =  0
      P1 in M :  I_{P1}(T ; Y | X)  =  c  >  0

      [ 0 . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . c ]
        ^                                         ^
        |                                         |
      min attained                             max attained

      The candidate's informational value depends
      entirely on which admissible model is true.
      Reporting only d+ WOULD BE A REPORTING ERROR.

  CASE 2: attributionally robust  ( d- > 0 )
  ---------------------------------------------
      all P in M :  I_P(T ; Y | X)  >  0

      [ d- . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . d+ ]
        ^                                         ^
      strictly positive everywhere

      This is the correct non-vacuity criterion.
```

